cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SILKern in academic work, please cite it. Author metadata is
  withheld pending peer review of the accompanying manuscript and will be
  filled in on de-anonymization; until then, cite the software release.
title: "SILKern: deterministic sparse-index localization for context-parallel decode"
abstract: >-
  Token-sparse decode selects global logical token positions while
  context-parallel attention consumes rank-owned physical KV-cache slots.
  Atomic-reservation converters between the two reserve output segments with atomic
  additions: they preserve the selected set and its cardinality but leave the
  order of the consumed prefix unspecified, so it varies across runs of
  identical input. SILKern provides an exact localization contract, an
  independent CPU oracle, and two allocation-free Triton implementations
  (row-wide and hierarchical) that additionally preserve the selector's global
  order and hold fixed addresses across CUDA-graph replay. An optional MLX
  backend provides functional localization on Apple silicon using native MLX
  operations or a fused Metal kernel, with explicit backend-specific memory
  guarantees and reproducible local conformance and timing tools.
type: software
version: "2.0.0"
